    {
      "id": "GO-2026-6770",
      "kind": "accepted-risk-upstream-binary",
      "reason": "Accepted by the owner on 2026-10-20. Not a false positive: podman 5.8.2's Go module is compiled into /usr/bin/podman, quadlet and rootlessport, and DeskOS neither builds nor patches the vendor's binary, so the fix is the distribution's rebuild. A newer base was checked first and does not fix it yet: today's :10 and :latest both carry podman 5.8.2, and the fix is 5.8.8. The vulnerable path is `podman run` honouring an image annotation that disables sandboxing, so it is exercised when a user runs an untrusted image; DeskOS itself does not run untrusted images. This record makes the acceptance explicit and expires on the review date below.",
      "matches": [
